@startuml
title M-SH5 - Host wait/lock graph (SH2+ target, R-LOCK)
left to right direction
component "Host state / fence lock" as lock
component "Local journal + record transition\nimmutable intent / durable in-flight marker" as journal
component "Unlocked per-record in-flight operation\nbounded outbound I/O" as inflight
component "swarma-dispatcher\nhost_start / host_stop / withdrawal / reconciliation" as dispatcher
component "swarma-session-runner\nauthenticated input / readiness" as runner
component "Unlocked result handler" as result
lock --> journal : held only for local transition
journal --> inflight : release state lock before call
inflight --> dispatcher : synchronous wait; no state lock held
inflight --> runner : synchronous wait; no state lock held
dispatcher --> result : return / late result; no host state lock held
runner --> result : return / late result; no host state lock held
result --> lock : reacquire for fence / epoch / version revalidation
note bottom of lock
  Never hold its state lock across a synchronous call to another platform service.
  Lock-held wait graph: state lock -> local transition only; no remote wait edge.
  Therefore acyclic. Return/control-flow arrows do not denote lock-held waits.
  Singleton / process-ownership locks are exempt; do not release them mechanically.
end note
note bottom of inflight
  Durable transition capacity comes from protected control / journal / audit reserve.
  Producer output cannot consume reserve; retained debt survives replacement / retirement.
  Budgets / bounded refusal logging / storage-failure semantics unpublished (§7.20).
  Ownership tracked by durable per-record in-flight marker, not global lock across I/O.
  Cancel/fence withdrawal records intent promptly; mid-call withdrawal uses a second
  unlocked dispatcher call and claim/receipt interlock. Retain possibly executed claims.
  Fresh authority checks on authority-creating use; intent is not an authority cache.
  Unrelated records and status / stop remain reachable during a stalled call.
  R-WATCH stop is journaled by dispatcher; host records reason and parks / ends.
  R-ALLSTOP journals host delivery closure / bound-board snapshots without remote lock waits.
  Hold fences until confirmed absence; no automatic restart after either stop.
end note
note bottom of result
  Bind call to immutable arguments / record / daemon-instance and controller epochs.
  Stale result may resolve history; never reopens delivery / admission or cancelled start.
  Marker schema, bounds and epoch-binding formats would need publication (§7.2).
end note
legend bottom
  [[../spec/session-host.md#34-effects-fences-and-admission Spec §3.4: R-LOCK and wait/lock graph]]
  [[../spec/session-host.md#7-open-questions Spec §7: publication / qualification gates]]
endlegend
@enduml
